Remove the unconditional keep_running reset performed when run_edge_loop starts.

n2n 3.1.1 writes `*eee->keep_running = true` as the first statement of
run_edge_loop, which discards a stop request issued between edge_init and the
loop entry (a real race for Go callers that stop from another goroutine).

The Go binding sets keep_running itself and checks stop_requested before
entering the loop, so this assignment is no longer needed.

--- a/src/edge_utils.c
+++ b/src/edge_utils.c
@@ -2895,7 +2895,6 @@ int run_edge_loop (n2n_edge_t *eee) {
 #endif
 
-    *eee->keep_running = true;
     update_supernode_reg(eee, time(NULL));
 
     /* Main loop
     *
